---
layout: base.njk
title: Deviations
permalink: /deviations/
---
<h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Deviations</h1>

<p class="govuk-body-l">
  Everything this library does differently from GOV.UK Frontend or from the
  published Defra branding guidance, and why.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Generated from <code>deviations.json</code>, which is the same file the drift
  check reads. A deviation that is not in that file fails the build, so this page
  is the whole list rather than a summary of it.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Markup deviations</h2>
<p class="govuk-body-s">
  Checked mechanically: the drift check renders all 692 upstream fixtures and
  fails on any divergence that is not declared here.
</p>
{% for name, d in system.deviations.components %}
  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">{{ d.id }} — {{ name | title }}</h3>
  <dl class="govuk-summary-list govuk-body-s">
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Reason</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.reason }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Approved by</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.approvedBy }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Review</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.review }}</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
{% endfor %}

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Design deviations</h2>
<p class="govuk-body-s">
  These cannot be caught by comparing markup, so the drift check prints them
  rather than asserting them. Printing is the point: an unassertable deviation
  must still be visible to a reviewer.
</p>
{% for name, d in system.deviations.design %}
  <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">{{ d.id }} — {{ name | title }}</h3>
  <dl class="govuk-summary-list govuk-body-s">
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Deviates from</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value"><a class="govuk-link" href="{{ d.deviatesFrom }}">{{ d.deviatesFrom }}</a></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Requirement</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.requirement }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">What we do</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value"><code>{{ d.actual }}</code></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Reason</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.reason }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Risk</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.risk }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
      <dt class="govuk-summary-list__key">Approved by</dt>
      <dd class="govuk-summary-list__value">{{ d.approvedBy }}</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
{% endfor %}

<h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Additions</h2>
<p class="govuk-body-s">
  Components with no upstream equivalent. Each records why GOV.UK Frontend has
  none, the cross-government work it follows rather than invents, and whether it
  has been proposed back.
</p>
<table class="govuk-table govuk-body-s">
  <thead class="govuk-table__head">
    <tr class="govuk-table__row">
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Reference</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Component</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Prior art</th>
      <th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Proposed upstream</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class="govuk-table__body">
    {% for name, d in system.deviations.additions %}
      {% if d.id %}
      <tr class="govuk-table__row">
        <th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">{{ d.id }}</th>
        <td class="govuk-table__cell"><a class="govuk-link" href="{{ '/components/' | url }}#{{ name }}">{{ name | title }}</a></td>
        <td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ d.priorArt }}</td>
        <td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ d.proposedUpstream }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
